WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.880
Today we are going to have a look&nbsp;
at the newest features Midjourney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:15.000
a text to image AI offers. Note that this&nbsp;
somewhat similar to Stable Diffusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.500
an open text to image AI that we can run at&nbsp;
home for free, but here, a subscription is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.000
required. Some of them cost quite a bit. So, is&nbsp;
it worth it? And what do we get for this money?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.860
Well, I would say two words:&nbsp;
quality and convenience.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:41.700
Let’s talk about quality first. If we asked&nbsp;
Midjourney version 1, just a bit more than a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:48.000
year ago for a scene with desert dunes, and&nbsp;
camels in front of The Great Sphinx of Giza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.960
we got something like this. Or this. But,&nbsp;
when asking version 5 to create the same,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:03.420
we get this. Now that is an incredible improvement&nbsp;
in just one year. However, in the prompt, we also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:10.200
asked for a highly-stylized result, and it seems&nbsp;
to have ignored that. Also, these images have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:18.720
some artifacting, and the camels feel a little&nbsp;
copy-pasty. Hmm, yes. It’s almost as if just one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:26.760
or two camel types were copied over many times.&nbsp;
No matter, because version 5.2 is already out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:33.480
and it fixed that that too. And the results&nbsp;
are breathtaking, stylized results. Loving it.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.460
And when asking for a high-contrast&nbsp;
surreal collage, with version 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:47.100
we got something like this. While version 5.2 is&nbsp;
a little more imaginative. I like this one a great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:54.360
deal better. Now, as a counterexample, when asking&nbsp;
for vibrant california poppies, the results are a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:01.200
toss up. These could easily pass for two images&nbsp;
from the same model. And both are excellent.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.920
So this was about quality, and Midjourney&nbsp;
has a great deal to offer when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.080
convenience. For instance, whenever we create&nbsp;
an image, and we are happy with the result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:20.640
but not with the framing, we can now also ask it&nbsp;
to zoom out. If we have an eye, we can say okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:30.900
but whose eye is this? And there we go. Fantastic.&nbsp;
And we can not only zoom, but we can also do some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:39.240
panning. Little AI, tell me, what’s next to this&nbsp;
creepy guy? Oh yes, of course, another creepy guy.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.780
And there are a tons more&nbsp;
convenience features in this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.660
for instance, it supports prompt weights.&nbsp;
For instance, if we ask for a wooden teapot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:55.020
we can even put more emphasis on the wood&nbsp;
part. And we get this. More like wood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.020 --> 00:03:02.460
less like a teapot. And then even more. Note&nbsp;
that the free Stable Diffusion can also do this.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:09.000
It also supports one of my favorites&nbsp;
for productivity: permutation prompts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.760
This is really underrated. If we are sure&nbsp;
that we wish to get a painting of a bird,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:21.720
but we are not quite sure which bird,&nbsp;
we can add multiple birds in the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:27.600
prompt. This will give us all four bird types&nbsp;
without having to create four prompts for it.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:34.560
And for the first sight, this does not seem like&nbsp;
a big thing, but this really is. Especially that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:41.400
Midjourney supports multiple permutations, and&nbsp;
even nested ones. With this, we can try out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:50.580
tens of ideas with just one prompt. An incredible&nbsp;
multiplier for your brain. I absolutely love this.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:58.440
And finally, it can also help us shorten our&nbsp;
prompts. What is that? Well, if we have tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:06.480
out way too many ideas and have a big bloated&nbsp;
prompt, it can help us sort out what parts of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:13.560
actually matter. Then, it gives us 5 new prompts&nbsp;
that are progressively shorter and shorter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.900
but all of them will try to retain the&nbsp;
heart and soul of the original one.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.480
So, these are some of the cooler features&nbsp;
of Midjourney, there are so many of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.760
for instance, we haven’t even talked&nbsp;
about Remix mode, and more. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.660
what do you think? Are you using&nbsp;
Midjourney? Is it worth the money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:39.180
or is it free Stable Diffusion all the way&nbsp;
for you? Let me know in the comments below!

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.300
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

